# The running world: always rebuilt with `nati seed --reset`
var/

# Traces are generated locally. Only curated examples are committed.
traces/*
!traces/examples/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Never: the Bedrock key can incur spend
.env
*.key

# Machine-local agent settings. Holds absolute paths from one developer's
# machine, so it is noise at best and broken at worst on a teammate's clone.
.claude/

# Working notes, not deliverables. Nothing matches these today — they exist so
# scratch never lands by accident. The things that ARE committed on purpose:
# README.md (how to run it), docs/SOP.md (the rules a break is judged against),
# docs/GLOSSARY.md, sealed/README.md, and the traces/examples READMEs.
CHEATSHEET*
NOTES*
SCRATCH*
TODO*
SUMMARY*
PLAN*.md
IMPLEMENTATION*.md
*_NOTES.md
*.local.md

# Domain values still to confirm with the administrator: an internal list.
OPEN_QUESTIONS.md

# Editor and OS cruft
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Coverage
.coverage
htmlcov/
